direction: down

title: |md
  ### FIB: Forwarding
  ### Information Base
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

flow: "Lookup input: flowi4" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  f_body: |md
    flowi4 lookup key:

    - daddr (dest IP)
    - saddr (src IP, may be 0)
    - tos / DSCP
    - oif (out iface, may be 0)
    - iif (in iface, may be 0)
    - flowi4_mark (skb mark)

    Lookup runs against a fib_table.
  |
}

trie: "fib_trie: LC-trie data structure" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  t_body: |md
    LC-trie (level-compressed
    trie) for the routing table.

    - Path-compressed: skip
    - &nbsp;&nbsp;single-child levels
    - Branch factor adapts
    - &nbsp;&nbsp;to data density
    - Lookup O(W), W = key
    - &nbsp;&nbsp;bits (32 for IPv4)
    - ~5-15 memory accesses
    - &nbsp;&nbsp;per lookup

    See net/ipv4/fib_trie.c
    (fib_table_lookup)
  |
}

result: "Result: struct fib_result" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  r_body: |md
    Lookup returns:

    - prefixlen of the match
    - nhc: next hop
    - &nbsp;&nbsp;(fib_nh_common)
    - type: UNICAST, LOCAL,
    - &nbsp;&nbsp;BROADCAST, MULTICAST
    - tclassid
    - table id

    Wrappers build a
    dst_entry / rtable:

    - ip_route_input
    - ip_route_output_flow
  |
}

flow -> trie -> result
